I see the array lookups in `pj_init_ctx` (pj_list), `pj_ell_set` (pj_ellps), and `pj_datum_set` (pj_datums). These all use the pattern:
```c
for (i = 0; (s = pj_list[i].id) && strcmp(name, s) ; ++i) ;
if (!s) { ... }
```

These arrays are null-terminated, so the loop stops at the null entry. The issue "array lookup with wrong indices due to missing validation before accessing the array" is a known OSS-Fuzz issue in proj.4. Let me look at the known issue. This is likely CVE-2018-... in proj.4. Let me search for the specific known bug.

The known OSS-Fuzz issue in proj.4 around this time (2017-2018) was in `pj_init.c` related to the `pj_list` lookup. Actually, let me look at the `pj_units` array lookup in `pj_init_ctx`:

```c
s = 0;
if ((name = pj_param(ctx, start, "sunits").s) != NULL) {
    for (i = 0; (s = pj_units[i].id) && strcmp(name, s) ; ++i) ;
    if (!s) { pj_ctx_set_errno( ctx, -7 ); goto bum_call; }
    s = pj_units[i].to_meter;
}
```

Let me check `pj_units` definition. Let me look at `pj_units.c`:

